From c6b2d15e9f2472edce41659a21303bcf281671e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:25:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(motion): enter each solid pass start by the asked
 entry in the pocket family

A 2D Adaptive (and Pocket, rest 2D) gave the helix entry only to the
first pass of the path and of each level. Each other pass start - a
second piece of the area, a ring its neighbours had not cleared - was
entered by a straight plunge into material, with no note, for a
centre-cutting tool.

- pass_link: when the ladder opts in (Motion::with_solid_restart) and
  the user asked for a helix, ramp or arc entry, a pass start in
  material (plunge_law::into_solid) is entered by entry_restart: the
  asked arm where it closes on or links to the start, else a ramp along
  the pass, else a plunge. Each stand-in is named with the site, level
  Z and reason.
- pocket_hsm: each piece after the first gets its own helix seed from
  choose_entry, not a bare axial dive.
- Plunges into a cleared column or air, Plunge entries and the rule for
  tools that are not centre-cutting are unchanged.

Pinned by crates/motion/tests/adaptive_entry_pieces.rs.

Fixes #2265

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
